## Summary

Ponytail review of `analysis/4-sim-bw-est-norm.qmd`.

The main issue was that estimator rows were each simulating their own dataset. That makes the ordinary-vs-normalised and cell-cap comparisons noisier than necessary, because differences in the output can come from different simulated cells rather than the estimator setting being compared.

This PR:
- derives the simulation seed from the biological scenario, so ordinary/normalised HPI methods and cell-cap settings are evaluated on the same simulated data;
- makes the requested HPI/HPI-Norm comparison explicit and fixes the development filter that effectively selected only `hpi1Norm`;
- keeps finite estimator failures visible through coverage/fallback summaries instead of averaging them away;
- records fallback provenance so a row is not silently labelled as the requested normalised method when a fallback path was used;
- makes simulation runs deterministic across chunking and worker scheduling;
- uses read-only canonical results when simulations are disabled;
- collates only the active chunk before promotion, validates exact IDs/errors/seeds/row counts, and validates the complete staged grid before promotion;
- handles empty chunks transactionally;
- restores the caller's future plan and avoids shared plotting during active multi-chunk renders;
- removes Quarto error masking from the transactional collation path;
- adds regression coverage and records the paired-estimator rule in `AGENTS.md`.

## Validation

The analysis integration workflow and R CMD check should exercise the updated QMD contract on CI.

## Scope

This is the smallest isolated implementation of the maintainer-requested Silent Payments boundary. The design document was committed before code changes.

### Architecture

```text
WAM node / block source
  -> Silent Payments scanner
  -> minimal scan/index SQLite state
  -> matched output metadata
  -> coordinator wallet
  -> offline Signer(Keyring)
```

- node/block source owns chain truth;
- scanner receives scan secret + spend public key only;
- scanner never receives the seed or spend private key;
- wallet coordinator owns coin/accounting/reservation flow but no spend secret;
- signing remains under `Signer(Keyring)` / the existing offline signer;
- no WAM Core `src/wallet/` changes and no invasive `patch_upstream.py` integration.

### Implementation

- adds structural `BlockSource` protocol with only `attest()` and `call()`;
- types scanner sync/mempool sync and public WSP scan API against that capability;
- replaces source/attribute-name boundary checks with a runtime proof: a non-empty Silent Payments scan and coordinator balance read execute while `Keyring.spend_secret` is forced to raise;
- documents that compromise of the scan secret exposes incoming-payment privacy but does not grant spending authority;
- documents the boundary in `docs/SILENT_PAYMENTS_ARCHITECTURE.md` and `SCANNER.md`.

Existing BIP-352/conformance tests remain unchanged and authoritative.

